.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt LS 1
.Os FreeLinX
.Sh NAME
.Nm ls
.Nd list directory contents
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm ls
.Op Fl AaCdfFimRrtu1
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists the contents of the named directories and the names of the
named files.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Include entries whose names begin with a dot (`.`).
.It Fl F
Display a trailing indicator for special files.
.It Fl l
List in long format, including permissions, owner, size, and date.
.It Fl R
Recursively list subdirectories.
.It Fl r
Reverse the sort order.
.It Fl t
Sort by time modified instead of by name.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cat 1 ,
.Xr cp 1 ,
.Xr stat 2
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
command appeared in Version&nbsp;1 AT&amp;T UNIX.